1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,800
This seller just let an AI agent refund customers on its own.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:13,200
Only for damaged items, only after the parcel is back,
and only because the agent passed that case five out of five times.

3
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:18,200
One refund goes through.

4
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:24,800
The next one crosses the daily limit and goes back to the seller.

5
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:30,200
Meet ReturnLens, the support agent that earns its autonomy.

6
00:00:30,600 --> 00:00:39,800
Small Indian sellers spend their day answering "where is my order",
returns and refunds across chat, courier panels and store policy.

7
00:00:40,200 --> 00:00:44,500
A customer asks where her order is.

8
00:00:44,800 --> 00:00:51,500
The agent calls our mock store and courier tools
and answers from live data.

9
00:00:52,000 --> 00:01:04,500
When the courier reports a failed delivery on a cash-on-delivery order,
the agent messages the buyer first, takes the corrected address,
and requests a re-delivery.

10
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:09,200
Now a harder one.
A buyer sends a voice note and an unboxing video.

11
00:01:09,600 --> 00:01:17,800
ReturnLens transcribes the request and checks the order:
white headphones. At 00:05 the video shows black ones.

12
00:01:18,200 --> 00:01:25,500
It does not call this fraud and does not guess the model number.
It marks the barcode as unverified.

13
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:35,500
It asks once for a photo of the box label,
and drafts the reply.

14
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:49,500
The seller sees every source and decides.

15
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:59,800
If the buyer leaves and comes back later,
the agent remembers the case, the language and what it already asked...

16
00:02:00,200 --> 00:02:09,500
...so it never asks twice.

17
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:16,000
Autonomy is not a setting we hand out.

18
00:02:16,400 --> 00:02:24,000
Every case type runs five times in a harness that checks the database,
the procedure and the message.

19
00:02:24,400 --> 00:02:29,200
8 of 10 scenarios passed all five runs.

20
00:02:29,600 --> 00:02:34,800
Anything below five out of five stays locked.
And one switch takes all autonomy back.

21
00:02:35,200 --> 00:02:39,500
Models observe.
Tools act on mock Shopify, Razorpay and Shiprocket-style contracts.

22
00:02:39,800 --> 00:02:47,500
Code enforces the money limits.
Every tool call, approval and block is logged.

23
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:59,500
ReturnLens.
Every return decision, backed by evidence.
